{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to datetime parsing capabilities, including support for C standard format codes and flexible timezone handling. It also expands the Parser class to support decimal grouping characters and hyphens in field names, while exposing new internal utilities for regex generation.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The public function dt_format_to_regex must be exposed to allow dynamic creation of regex patterns from C standard datetime format codes. The Parser class must handle single-digit days and months, allow colons in time formats, and support flexible parsing of %z while shielding Python 2 from specific timezone features."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The classes FixedTzOffset, RepeatedNameError, and the functions date_convert and extract_format must remain accessible as part of the stable public API following structural refactoring."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "The Parser class must expose a formatter property that allows access to the formatting logic associated with the parsed result."
    },
    {
      "id": "m24",
      "text": "Datetime parsing for the %f directive must support various numbers of digits after the comma, ensuring consistent behavior regardless of fractional second precision."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26",
      "text": "The Parser class and extract_format function must allow hyphen-minus characters within field names during pattern matching and extraction."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The Parser class and extract_format function must support grouping characters (commas and underscores) in decimal format strings for proper number parsing."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are correctly exported and behave according to these specifications before tagging the next version."
}
